# IntelliJ. Nothing under .idea/ is tracked anywhere in this repository, so it was
# meant to be ignored and never was. It shows up as untracked noise on every status.
.idea/

# Yarn PnP, run through Corepack from the `packageManager` field. The install state and the
# resolution maps are produced by `yarn install` and are not committed, because the cache they
# point into is not committed either. A `node_modules` directory or a `package-lock.json` means
# the wrong package manager was used; `package-lock.json` is left visible on purpose.
node_modules/
.pnp.cjs
.pnp.loader.mjs
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions

# Build output, produced by `yarn build`.
/dist
